# Shape the published source archive. GitHub builds the /archive/*.zip download and the release source
# tarballs with `git archive`, which honors `export-ignore`, and that archive is exactly what SymBot's
# self-updater downloads and installs. Paths marked below stay in the repository — so continuous
# integration, the pre-commit hook, and anyone who clones still have them — but they are left OUT of the
# distributed archive, so a running instance's upgrade never installs files the runtime does not need. A
# fresh `git clone` is unaffected and still contains everything.
#
# This is kept in step with the Docker build's .dockerignore so the self-update install and the Docker image
# agree on what ships. For the archive to be shaped this way, .gitattributes must be committed and present at
# the release tag.
#
# scripts/ is intentionally KEPT in the archive: run-tests.js is written to exit gracefully with "no tests
# bundled" when libs/test/ is absent, so `npm test` / `npm run check` behave (and precheck.js can syntax-check
# the shipped libs/) on an installed copy. Only the bulk test suite (libs/test/) and dev-only hook/CI dirs are
# excluded.
libs/test          export-ignore
.githooks          export-ignore
